--------------- WELCOME TO THE TERMINAL ON CANFAR -------------------

Rubin Observatory Science Platform Notebook Aspect running and
configured for CANFAR.  If you have issues please contact:
	   support@canfar.net

Service discovery is populated at session start from
https://www.canfar.net/storage/arc/file/projects/LSST/cadc_dataset_map.yaml
(override with CANFAR_DATASET_MAP) via the CADC resource-caps registry into
/etc/nublado/discovery/v1.json.  Your CADC access token
is published where RSPDiscovery expects it
(/etc/nublado/secrets/token, NUBLADO_TOKEN, ACCESS_TOKEN).

List discovery dataset labels and Butler repository aliases:

        from lsst.rsp import list_datasets, RSPDiscovery
        from lsst.daf.butler import Butler
        list_datasets()
        sorted(Butler.get_known_repos())

Example (CANFAR YouCAT / CAOM services):

        discovery = RSPDiscovery("dp2")
        tap = discovery.get_tap_client()

Firefly: use the JupyterLab launcher card "Firefly Viewer" (Firefly
section).  It starts a CANFAR Firefly session if needed and opens it
in a Lab tab.  Tutorials: use the Tutorials menu.  It lists Rubin's
lsst/tutorial-notebooks@main plus a CANFAR submenu from the sciplat-lab/
folder of ijiraq/canfar-tutorials (set by CANFAR_TUTORIALS_REPO).

Rubin services (rubin-dp2, rubin-dp1, dp02, prompt) and HiPS URLs on
dp1/dp2 point at data.lsst.cloud and need a Rubin token.  Create one at
https://data.lsst.cloud/settings/tokens (scopes read:tap, read:image),
save it once with:

        rubin-login

then in a notebook:

        from canfar_tokens import rubin_token
        rubin = RSPDiscovery("rubin-dp2", token=rubin_token())
        butler = Butler("rubin-dp2", collections=["dp2"])

See Welcome.md for the full recipe.


